# Fuzz crashers are deliberately not committed.
#
# Go replays testdata/fuzz/<Target>/* as seeds on every plain `go test`, so a
# committed crasher is a permanently failing test. That is the right outcome
# for a defect we can fix — and the wrong one for a defect in an upstream
# dependency that we cannot.
#
# Crashers for unresolved third-party defects are kept out of the repository
# entirely rather than merely out of the corpus. See README.md.
testdata/fuzz/
